{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1162964-need-tips-on-running-a-vtm20-dtf-crossover-chronicle","id":1162964,"title":"Need tips on running a VtM20 + DtF crossover chronicle","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-27T05:36:38-08:00","id":1162964,"title":"Need tips on running a VtM20 + DtF crossover chronicle","content":"Pretty much what the title says. Me and a friend decided to run a chronicle set in Paris(the year being the current year) where we will crossover VtM and DtF. They play a vampire while I'll be playing a demon. I'll put some details below about where we are so far.<br /> <br /> Since DtF hasn't been updated to present day standards, I figured I'd ask for a few tips on what might need to be updated or altered to work better with the VtM stuff and vice versa(as I've seen people comment that some DtF stuff wasn't properly thought out when reading about it in the past). Also if there's any info on kindred in Paris beyond the entry on the wiki talking about the Prince of Paris.<br /> <br /> We're currently running with the idea that the fallen are still largely unknown to the kindred with only a few of them being aware of the fallen and their real nature. In addition that their presence in Paris can be counted on one hand at the moment since we're starting with a heavy focus on VtM first(In terms of sects, we're using the Camarilla and independents with the sabbat as an enemy).<br /> <br /> Currently we're not using much in the way of house rules beyond some decisions on how other parts of oWoD lore factors into the crossover(gehenna was averted for example with no one knowing how, the withering is over, all pentex staff will be arrested and put on trial after someone remembered to bring a cellphone to document the stuff I hear they keep doing, etc) and that we started char gen with more freebie points and some XP. We were also discussing how a fallens Faith based abilities and spells might work on kindred given that vampires seem to handle Faith based stuff rather poorly. So any thoughts on that would be quite welcome.<br /> <br /> All in all any tips, suggestions and such are appreciated. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T11:36:58-08:00","id":1163294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amalasuintha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1162964-need-tips-on-running-a-vtm20-dtf-crossover-chronicle#post1162964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since DtF hasn't been updated to present day standards, I figured I'd ask for a few tips on what might need to be updated or altered to work better with the VtM stuff and vice versa(as I've seen people comment that some DtF stuff wasn't properly thought out when reading about it in the past). Also if there's any info on kindred in Paris beyond the entry on the wiki talking about the Prince of Paris.<br /> <br /> We're currently running with the idea that the fallen are still largely unknown to the kindred with only a few of them being aware of the fallen and their real nature. In addition that their presence in Paris can be counted on one hand at the moment since we're starting with a heavy focus on VtM first(In terms of sects, we're using the Camarilla and independents with the sabbat as an enemy).</div> </div> </div> </div>None really. I may think that a lot of rules of DtF need improving, but they're as compatible with vampire as they can be. You even have &quot;virtues&quot;.<br /> <br /> Torment it's mechanically similar to Humaity, but inversed. You may use it that way, I guess.<br /> <br /> You MAY want to consider that True Faith doesn't exist in DtF as a Merit/Numina-you will have to decide how this thing will relate to Demon, if it exists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We were also discussing how a fallens Faith based abilities and spells might work on kindred given that vampires seem to handle Faith based stuff rather poorly. So any thoughts on that would be quite welcome. </div> </div> </div>Demons don't react well to faith based offenses either. Think about what demons suffer in holly ground when their Torment it's relatively high, or when struck by blessed weapons. There's a section of &quot;<b>faith as a weapon</b>&quot; that describes how faith can be used against the Fallen-and you don't even need to have True Faith to use it (well, the Merit doesn't exist in Demon, so it's no surprise)<br /> Vampires and demons react to faith differently, but there's no reason to think demonic faith based powers are going to be more effective on them (than against anyone else's). Other than, perhaps, rewarding a particularly devout demonic thrall with True Faith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-28-2017, 02:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T17:33:48-08:00","id":1163409,"title":"","content":"I've been there sometimes, running Demons and Vampires in the same chronicle, or playing a Demon in a Vampire chronicle. So, here's my advice.<br /> <br /> First: True Faith = Faith rating -3. Most people don't have True Faith, but they still have a Faith rating from 1 to 3 for Demons' standards. Someone with actual True Faith should have this rating +3 as Faith for Demon's purposes. Let them react by their own rules against this Faith.<br /> <br /> Second: keep Vampires out of thralldom. For whatever reason, an Undead can't enter a full Pact. At most, such a Pact should only let the Demon give leeway for the Vampire to buy stuff without a formal preparation. So maybe the Demon can empower a Vampire to learn a Discipline without a teacher. But keep them out of the normal rules to evade serious problems with XP economy. Those problems can easily translate to too much power in the hands of the Demon.<br /> <br /> Third: keep Vampires from doing too much with Faith. You can make Demons ignore a Vampire's Faith rating, you can make them sufficiently resilient against the Faith of the Leeches to use only the True Faith rating in such situations. That will keep the Vampires from overwhelming the Demon when they learn about this and make Ghouls into proxies for such methods, as they are among Vampires already, and Thralls are among Demons.<br /> <br /> And Fourth: take a pause to consider some aspects and answer some questions with the chronicles themes in mind. A mortal can be both a Ghoul and a Thrall? Can a Vampire's Faith refresh a Demon outside of a Pact? If a Pact is made, can the Demon still inflict Ravage upon the Vampire? Such questions aren't a big deal from a balance standpoint, but each possible answer will open and close avenues for stories, so they are up to the ST.<br /> <br /> Regarding the problems with Demon's rules, they're not so much a cross-over problem. You can experience unbalance, certainly, in unpredictable ways, but they mostly blend nicely. The problem is more of Demon itself not being as well developed as anything else in WoD, so it will be there once you use DtF's rules, cross-over or not. If you want, you can take a look into Devil's Due. It is Dark Age of sorts for Demon, but is actually a Vampire's book, so the rules are already VtM. I'm not a fan, and it isn't guaranteed balance to actually play a mixed game, but maybe they are to your liking. My four rules above worked good enough for me, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T06:50:28-08:00","id":1163530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1162964-need-tips-on-running-a-vtm20-dtf-crossover-chronicle?p=1163294#post1163294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> None really. I may think that a lot of rules of DtF need improving, but they're as compatible with vampire as they can be. You even have &quot;virtues&quot;.<br /> <br /> Torment it's mechanically similar to Humaity, but inversed. You may use it that way, I guess.<br /> <br /> You MAY want to consider that True Faith doesn't exist in DtF as a Merit/Numina-you will have to decide how this thing will relate to Demon, if it exists.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Demons don't react well to faith based offenses either. Think about what demons suffer in holly ground when their Torment it's relatively high, or when struck by blessed weapons. There's a section of &quot;<b>faith as a weapon</b>&quot; that describes how faith can be used against the Fallen-and you don't even need to have True Faith to use it (well, the Merit doesn't exist in Demon, so it's no surprise)<br /> Vampires and demons react to faith differently, but there's no reason to think demonic faith based powers are going to be more effective on them (than against anyone else's). Other than, perhaps, rewarding a particularly devout demonic thrall with True Faith.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1162964-need-tips-on-running-a-vtm20-dtf-crossover-chronicle?p=1163409#post1163409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been there sometimes, running Demons and Vampires in the same chronicle, or playing a Demon in a Vampire chronicle. So, here's my advice.<br /> <br /> First: True Faith = Faith rating -3. Most people don't have True Faith, but they still have a Faith rating from 1 to 3 for Demons' standards. Someone with actual True Faith should have this rating +3 as Faith for Demon's purposes. Let them react by their own rules against this Faith.</div> </div> </div> </div>We've been treating True Faith as mortals(or vampires in some rare cases) as its owner being able to use its Divine Spark in some fashion so far. We've not run into someone that can do it yet granted. As for Faith as a weapon, I figured the reason it is like that was more a case of the Faith used simply being aimed that way. So if they both have issues with it, they might react to it similarly. The advices are good though we'll keep it in mind for when we run into it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1162964-need-tips-on-running-a-vtm20-dtf-crossover-chronicle?p=1163409#post1163409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Second: keep Vampires out of thralldom. For whatever reason, an Undead can't enter a full Pact. At most, such a Pact should only let the Demon give leeway for the Vampire to buy stuff without a formal preparation. So maybe the Demon can empower a Vampire to learn a Discipline without a teacher. But keep them out of the normal rules to evade serious problems with XP economy. Those problems can easily translate to too much power in the hands of the Demon.</div> </div> </div> </div> One of the sourcebooks did mention something about this. Mostly that vampires can't be thralls IIRC, but can make pacts(at storyteller discretion I think?). We'll see if we can figure out a way to deal with it should it come up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1162964-need-tips-on-running-a-vtm20-dtf-crossover-chronicle?p=1163409#post1163409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Third: keep Vampires from doing too much with Faith. You can make Demons ignore a Vampire's Faith rating, you can make them sufficiently resilient against the Faith of the Leeches to use only the True Faith rating in such situations. That will keep the Vampires from overwhelming the Demon when they learn about this and make Ghouls into proxies for such methods, as they are among Vampires already, and Thralls are among Demons.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sounds like a useful idea. We'll probably do it in a similar fashion. Will have to see what we agree on when we discuss it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1162964-need-tips-on-running-a-vtm20-dtf-crossover-chronicle?p=1163409#post1163409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Fourth: take a pause to consider some aspects and answer some questions with the chronicles themes in mind. A mortal can be both a Ghoul and a Thrall? Can a Vampire's Faith refresh a Demon outside of a Pact? If a Pact is made, can the Demon still inflict Ravage upon the Vampire? Such questions aren't a big deal from a balance standpoint, but each possible answer will open and close avenues for stories, so they are up to the ST.</div> </div> </div> </div> At the moment in regards to ghouls and thralls, we're going with what one of the sourcebooks said. Namely that a mortal can be one or the other, but not both. Figured it'd be easier to handle that way. We've not thought about ravaging yet however. I'll be showing this thread to my friend though so they can tell me what they think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1162964-need-tips-on-running-a-vtm20-dtf-crossover-chronicle?p=1163409#post1163409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the problems with Demon's rules, they're not so much a cross-over problem. You can experience unbalance, certainly, in unpredictable ways, but they mostly blend nicely. The problem is more of Demon itself not being as well developed as anything else in WoD, so it will be there once you use DtF's rules, cross-over or not. If you want, you can take a look into Devil's Due. It is Dark Age of sorts for Demon, but is actually a Vampire's book, so the rules are already VtM. I'm not a fan, and it isn't guaranteed balance to actually play a mixed game, but maybe they are to your liking. My four rules above worked good enough for me, though.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thanks for the suggestion. I went and got ahold of that book. Should be useful down the road once I've read it and seen what I can use in it. As for balance, right now we're going a bit rules light and power heavy in the mechanics department since we're going mostly for a story feel. That and my memory is very poor due to some health issues so rules light helps a bit.<br /> <br /> Also wanted to thank both of you for your tips. They've given me stuff to ponder on. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}